 "notes": "Blue solid FIRAS curve (B0_rms = 1 nG, the CMB upper bound on scale-invariant primordial magnetic fields) from Fig. 13 (eps/gagg_constraints.pdf), extracted from the vector paths of the figure PDF with axes calibrated on the gridlines. 95% c.l. COBE/FIRAS spectral-distortion limit computed with CosmoTherm; the paper derives this bound itself from a re-analysis of FIRAS data, so it is a new measured limit (the red PIXIE curve is a forecast and was not used). The y-axis is f*g_agamma where f = B_rms,T/B0_rms is an O(1) geometric fudge factor (naive angle-averaging gives f = 1/3); the curve is reported as plotted, i.e. effectively f = 1. Not a dark-matter search (bound is on gamma->a conversion of CMB photons, Omega_a << 1), so no rho_DM rescaling applies.",
